{
  "id": "ep118",
  "duration": 48.332,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.104,
      "text": "One tiny moon looks like a jigsaw puzzle glued back together.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda as seen by Voyager 2 - GPN-2003-000005.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_as_seen_by_Voyager_2_-_GPN-2003-000005.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.104,
      "end": 11.974,
      "text": "When Voyager 2 reached Uranus in 1986, scientists expected its moon Miranda to be a boring ice-ball.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Uranus2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uranus2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.1,
          "end": 11.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.974,
      "end": 17.219,
      "text": "Instead, they found a patchwork 'Frankenstein' world with a massive V-shaped scar.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda as seen by Voyager 2 - GPN-2003-000005 (cropped).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_as_seen_by_Voyager_2_-_GPN-2003-000005_(cropped).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.967,
          "end": 14.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 14.6,
          "end": 17.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.219,
      "end": 23.469,
      "text": "Miranda\u2019s surface features Verona Rupes, a staggering cliff reaching up to twelve miles deep.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda scarp.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_scarp.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.233,
          "end": 20.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.333,
          "end": 23.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.469,
      "end": 28.664,
      "text": "That is twelve times deeper than the Grand Canyon, on a world the size of Texas.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "GrandCanyon.NASA.2014.jpg",
        "credit": "Astronaut photograph ISS039-E-5258; taken by the Expedition 39 crew of the International Space Station;",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GrandCanyon.NASA.2014.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.467,
          "end": 28.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.664,
      "end": 36.484,
      "text": "One leading theory suggests the moon was shattered by impacts multiple times before reassembling into a chaotic pile.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist's concept of collision at HD 172555.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%27s_concept_of_collision_at_HD_172555.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.667,
          "end": 34.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 34.033,
          "end": 36.5,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.484,
      "end": 44.234,
      "text": "Alternatively, extreme tidal heating from Uranus might have churned the moon's icy interior into these bizarre shapes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "11214 2023 990 Fig1 HTML.webp",
        "credit": "by David Hinkle (JPL)\n\nin Roberts, J.H., McKinnon, W.B., Elder, C.M.\u00a0et al.\u00a0Exploring the Interior of Europa with the Europa Clipper.\u00a0Space Sci Rev\u00a0219, 46 (2023). https://doi.org/10.1007/s11214-023-0",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:11214_2023_990_Fig1_HTML.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.5,
          "end": 44.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.234,
      "end": 47.982,
      "text": "With only the southern half ever photographed, nobody knows why.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Miranda as seen by Voyager 2 - GPN-2003-000005.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miranda_as_seen_by_Voyager_2_-_GPN-2003-000005.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.233,
          "end": 48.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
